@dramaticlly and @stevenzwu, I can explain a bit more about the rationale for changing this.

Anoop is working on an API for validations. Right now, we have quite a few methods in `MergingSnapshotProducer` that were added over time as we needed more validations. The idea for v4 is to introduce an API that we can configure so that it can validate v3 or earlier and v4 or later using different logic. For example, v4 is going to be different because validating there are no new deletes for a given data file requires finding the data file and checking its DV matches what was expected. In v3, we have to go through all new deletes, build indexes, and run data file matching.

In building an API for validations, we want to simplify where possible. Right now, each validation method like `validateNoNewDeletesForDataFiles` passes all of the requirements in, including `startingSnapshotId` and `conflictDetectionFilter`. Because the filter could differ across calls, the validator can't really cache. But if we update the API to pass those things just once, then it can cache decisions about snapshots and other work. That led to this PR because this is the only place where there are multiple expressi […]

The approach this PR takes is to try to unify all cases with a single conflict detection filter. As I said in my comment above, the goal is to be able to use a simpler API, like this:
```java
public validator() {
  // this would be built just once
  return Validator.newValidator()
      .io(table.io())
      .startingSnapshotId(startId)
      .conflictDetectionFilter(filter);
}

public void validate(TableMetadata base, Snapshot parent) {
  if (validateNewDataFiles) {
    validator.validateAddedDataFiles();
  }

  if (validateNewDeletes) {
    if (deleteByRowFilter) {
      // no new delete files for files removed by filter
      validator.validateNoNewDeleteFiles();
      // no files removed by filter are already deleted
      validator.validateDeletedDataFiles();
    }

    if (!deletedDataFiles.isEmpty()) {
      // no new delete files for files removed by deleteFile(...)
      validator.validateNoNewDeleteFilesFor(deletedDataFiles);
    }
  }
}
```

